      "latency_ms": 31698.3,
      "prompt_tokens": 18,
      "completion_tokens": 1151,
      "output": "At its most basic level, **water** is a chemical compound with the chemical formula **H₂O**. This means that each molecule of water is made up of two hydrogen atoms bonded to one oxygen atom.\n\nHere is a breakdown of what makes water unique and important:\n\n### 1. Chemical Structure\nWater is a **polar molecule**. Because oxygen is more electronegative (it pulls electrons more strongly) than hydrogen, the oxygen end of the molecule has a slight negative charge, and the hydrogen ends have a slight positive charge. This polarity allows water to stick to itself (cohesion) and to other substances (adhesion), which is why water can form droplets and flow.\n\n### 2. The Three States of Matter\nWater is unique because it is the only common substance found naturally on Earth in all three physical states:\n*   **Solid:** Ice (frozen water)\n*   **Liquid:** The state we use for drinking and washing\n*   **Gas:** Water vapor (invisible gas in the atmosphere)\n\n### 3. Unique Physical Properties\nWater has several properties that are essential for life and the planet:\n*   **High Surface Tension:** Water molecules stick together strongly at the surface, creating a kind of \"skin.\" This allows small insects to walk on water and helps plants pull water up from their roots.\n*   **Universal Solvent:** Water can dissolve more substances than any other liquid. This is why it is the main transport system in the human body (carrying nutrients) and in the environment (dissolving minerals in soil).\n*   **High Specific Heat:** Water can absorb a lot of heat before it gets hot, and release a lot of heat before it gets cold. This helps regulate the Earth's temperature, making life possible.\n\n### 4. Importance to Life\nWater is the foundation of life as we know it. It is a major component of all living cells (about 60% of the human body) and is necessary for:\n*   Chemical reactions in the body.\n*   Temperature regulation (sweating).\n*   Lubricating joints and organs.\n*   Transporting nutrients and waste.\n\nIn summary, water is a simple molecule (H₂O) that acts as a universal solvent and a temperature stabilizer, making it the essential medium for life on Earth."
